-- DICT-SEMANTICS §3 well-formedness W1: "the superclass relation is ACYCLIC --
-- otherwise `super`-search loops".
--
-- SPEC ANSWER (hand-derived): `P requires Q` and `Q requires P` is a cycle, so
-- W1 fails and entailment is not decidable. The program must be REJECTED, and
-- rejected STATICALLY -- a compiler that instead loops in `super`-search is the
-- failure W1 exists to forbid, and would show up here as a hang, not a verdict.
--
-- OBSERVED: check/run/build all REJECT with `T-CYCLIC-SUPERINTERFACE`
-- ("Cyclic superinterface: P requires Q requires P"). CONFORMANT.
--
-- The gate bounds every invocation at 60s, so a regression to the looping
-- behavior surfaces as a row failure rather than a hung CI job.
interface P a requires Q a where
  pm : a -> Int

interface Q a requires P a where
  qm : a -> Int

impl P Int where
  pm n = n

impl Q Int where
  qm n = n

main = println (pm (1 : Int))
